# Implementation summary

The repository now contains an Azure Developer CLI project that deploys a disposable Odoo/PostgreSQL/MCP stack behind Caddy HTTPS ingress in one Azure Container Instances container group.

## Files

- `azure.yaml`: azd infrastructure configuration, cross-platform hooks, and `azd deploy` reset behavior.
- `infra/main.bicep` and `infra/main.parameters.json`: subscription-scope resource group, azd parameter mapping, generated secrets, configurable images, and deployment outputs.
- `infra/modules/container-group.bicep`: ACI group, internal networking, ephemeral volumes, bootstrap orchestration, MCP configuration, and Caddy-only public ingress.
- `scripts/preprovision.*`: cross-platform image selection and optional ACR build orchestration.
- `scripts/build-images.*`: optional immutable ACR remote builds for all four image contexts.
- `scripts/postdelivery.*`: post-provision endpoints and demo credentials.
- `src/odoo-mcp`: authenticated Python MCP server, tests, and non-root multi-stage image.
- `src/odoo` and `src/postgres`: reproducible base-image build contexts.
- `src/caddy`: pinned Caddy image and HTTPS path-routing configuration.
- `README.md`: prerequisites, image contract, deployment/reset instructions, and security guidance.

```mermaid
graph LR
  ACR[External ACR] --> ACI[ACI container group]
  subgraph ACI
    DB[(PostgreSQL)]
    Init[Odoo bootstrap] --> DB
    Odoo[Odoo] --> DB
    MCP[MCP server] -->|JSON-RPC| Odoo
    Caddy[Caddy] -->|default| Odoo
    Caddy -->|/mcp| MCP
  end
  Internet -->|HTTPS 443| Caddy
```
